{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_9router_extraction_map", "label": "9Router to OptiAI Extraction Map", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L1-L7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Path-by-path record of the 422-file extraction from 9router-app v0.5.75, with retained, modified, added and excluded tables, and zero unresolved imports."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_import_graph_walk", "label": "Import-Graph Walk File Selection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L5-L36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 422 files were selected by walking the import graph transitively from OptiAI's entry points through relative, @/* and open-sse/* imports - not by copying directories - so every reachable file came along and nothing else."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_registry_not_subsettable", "label": "Provider Registry Cannot Be Subset", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "registry/index.js statically imports all 123 provider files, so any subset breaks the registry outright - the whole set is retained even though only 16 providers are reachable."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_executors_retained", "label": "Executors Retained for Binary Upstreams", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L46", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All 30 per-provider executors are kept because binary/protobuf upstreams cannot round-trip the translator."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_compact_naming_note", "label": "compact.js Naming Note", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L70-L73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "open-sse/services/compact.js is combo (model-combo) handling with fallback, NOT context compaction, despite the name. Real context compaction in 9Router is a _compact: true flag on the same chat pipeline (/v1/responses/compact), which OptiAI inherits for free via the gateway."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_nextresponse_shim", "label": "NextResponse to Response.json Shim", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L81-L83", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three route files only ever used NextResponse.json(), so a 1-line Response.json shim removes the next/server dependency from the backend."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_machineid_cjs_fix", "label": "node-machine-id CJS Import Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L84-L85", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "node-machine-id is CommonJS; Next's bundler resolved the named machineIdSync export but plain Node throws, so both machineId modules switch to a default import plus destructure."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_apikey_format", "label": "Gateway API Key Format sk-machine-id-crc", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L62-L63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Issued keys embed a salted stable machine id, tying CLI-to-OptiAI auth to the host machine."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_db_driver_chain", "label": "SQLite Driver Fallback Chain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L118-L119", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "bun:sqlite -> better-sqlite3 -> node:sqlite -> sql.js. On Node >=22.5 it resolves to node:sqlite; better-sqlite3 stays optional and sql.js is the pure-JS floor, so the app runs without a native build."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_provider_count_note", "label": "119 Catalog Entries vs 81 PROVIDERS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L115-L117", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "119 entries surface in the catalog while PROVIDERS (transport configs) has 81; the difference is registry entries that are media/other-category only."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_requireapikey_default", "label": "requireApiKey Defaults True in Imported Settings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L120-L121", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rather than flip the imported default off, OptiAI's internal /api/chat attaches a stored local key, keeping the gate's behaviour identical to upstream."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_package_json_version", "label": "Added backend/9router/package.json Version Marker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L88-L92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only added, non-upstream file: type: module plus a version field that open-sse/config/appConstants.js reads via createRequire(\"../../package.json\") for upstream User-Agent strings."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_excluded_dashboard_auth", "label": "Excluded Dashboard UI and Auth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L96-L112", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The whole (dashboard) UI, UI kit, Zustand stores and password/JWT/SAML/OIDC login are excluded because OptiAI builds its own UI and its auth is a separate, later design. MITM needs a root CA and admin rights, tunnels are unneeded locally, and upstream tests are not green on a plain checkout and are tied to its layout."}, {"id": "docs_9router_extraction_headroom_pxpipe_inert", "label": "Headroom / PXPIPE Kept Inert", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L61,L109", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "src/lib/headroom/detect.js and pxpipe modules came along only as rtk/ import dependencies; the sidecar-spawning code is excluded and no sidecar process is ever started."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_9router_extraction_map", "target": "readme_9router", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_import_graph_walk", "target": "docs_9router_extraction_map", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L5-L36", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_import_graph_walk", "target": "readme_extracted_9router_tree", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L5-L6", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_registry_not_subsettable", "target": "readme_provider_allowlist", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_registry_not_subsettable", "target": "readme_path_preservation", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L42", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_provider_count_note", "target": "readme_provider_allowlist", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L115-L117", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_provider_count_note", "target": "readme_usemodelcatalog", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L115", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_apikey_format", "target": "readme_cli_gateway", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L62", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_requireapikey_default", "target": "readme_requireapikey_autoattach", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L120-L121", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_nextresponse_shim", "target": "readme_extracted_9router_tree", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L81-L83", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_machineid_cjs_fix", "target": "docs_9router_extraction_apikey_format", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L62-L63,L84-L85", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_compact_naming_note", "target": "readme_chat_entry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/9router-extraction.md", "source_location": "L70-L73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_9router_extraction_compact_naming_note", "targe